     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hannah-<div><br></div><div>They don&#39;t look terrible to me. That amount of variability with n=25 and 43 is to be expected. You should try generating a n of 25 or 43 from the absolute value of a normal and then look at it with the intervals you used.</div><div><br></div><div>Here is one such picture. In R I used abs(rnorm(25,0,200)). You may be surprised by the variability. It does look like you may have some rounding to values 100, 200 etc but since you didn&#39;t say how distance was measured I&#39;m not sure if that is reasonable.</div><div><br></div><div>--jeff</div><div><br></div><div><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/22336ed3d4af6509/image.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"Inline image 1\" width=\"485\" height=\"282\"><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Apr 28, 2015 at 1:55 PM,  <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<div style=\"border:1px solid #d3d3d3;max-width:850px;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000\">\r\n  <div style=\"background-color:#f5f5f5;padding:10px 20px\">\r\n    <table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%\">\r\n      <tbody>\r\n        <tr>\r\n          <td style=\"width:70%\">\r\n            <span style=\"font:18px/20px arial;color:#333333\">\r\n              <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email#!forum/distance-sampling/topics\" style=\"text-decoration:none;color:#333333\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail%23!forum/distance-sampling/topics&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475989215000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1awdiCXWx-4JwIKcxMapgl\">\r\n              distance...@g